notes.content:
The concept of 'measurement error' can be used both

. when there is a single reference quantity value to refer to, which occurs if a {{2.39,calibration}}
is made by means of a {{5.1,measurement standard}} with a {{2.10,measured quantity value}} having
a negligible {{2.26,measurement uncertainty}} or if a {{2.12,conventional quantity value}}
is given, in which case the measurement error is known, and

. if a {{2.3,measurand}} is supposed to be represented by a unique {{2.11,true quantity value}}
or a set of true quantity values of negligible range, in which case the measurement error
is not known.
